  "solution": {
    "text": "Concept - Those compounds which are more acidic than $\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{CO}_3$ can gives effervescence of $\\mathrm{CO}_2$ with aq. $\\mathrm{NaHCO}_3$.<br />Release $\\mathrm{CO}_2 \\uparrow$ gas with aq. NaHCO 3<br />$\\Rightarrow[\\text { A.S. }]_{\\text {Comp. }} \\gt [\\text { A.S. }]_{\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{CO}_3}$<br />$\\rightarrow$ Option 1,2 and 3 gives effervescence of $\\mathrm{CO}_2$ gas with $\\mathrm{NaHCO}_3$<br />$\\rightarrow$ Option (4) Not gives $\\mathrm{CO}_2$ gas with $\\mathrm{NaHCO}_3$.",
